{"findings":[{"rule_id":"MC-009","evidence":[{"kind":"title_block","ref":"title","page":1,"quote":"PIN"},{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D4","page":1,"quote":"⌀15"},{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D8","page":1,"quote":"64"}],"comment":"The part is a 64 mm long, ⌀15 mm shaft (title block 'PIN', D4, D8) that would typically be turned between centres, yet no centre holes are specified. Without centre holes the machinist lacks a defined method to support and locate the shaft during turning, risking poor concentricity. The designer should add centre hole callouts on both ends or explicitly state an alternative machining method."

    ,
    "recommended_correction": "Add centre hole specifications (e.g., per ISO 6411) at both ends of the pin, or add a note defining how the shaft is to be supported during turning."}]}
